{"chunk_id": "f6108db8a070", "text": "Krishna explains the nature of devotion, cosmic cycles, and the supreme reality beyond rebirth. Those who meditate on him with single\u2011minded devotion can easily reach him and escape the cycle of birth and death that governs all worlds, even the highest heavenly realms. The universe repeatedly emerges from the unmanifest during Brahma\u2019s cosmic day and dissolves again at night, yet beyond this process exists an eternal, indestructible reality\u2014Krishna\u2019s supreme abode. He describes two post\u2011death paths: one leading to liberation and non\u2011return, the other to eventual rebirth. In the opening of Chapter IX, Krishna reveals the \u201croyal knowledge\u201d: he pervades the entire universe while remaining beyond it. True devotees recognize him as the origin and essence of all sacrifices, gods, and natural forces, offering every action to him and thereby transcending karma.\nKrishna explains cosmic cycles, the paths after death, and reveals the royal knowledge that devotion to him transcends rituals and leads to liberation.\nThemes: cosmic cycles, paths after death, divine immanence, bhakti devotion, transcending ritualism", "vector": [0.012332126498222351, 0.009397458285093307, -0.004913938231766224, 0.003286828054115176, -0.015729820355772972, 0.006511701736599207, -0.021742628887295723, -0.016277624294161797, -0.025290315970778465, 0.013160355389118195, 0.0014714098069816828, 0.01014090795069933, -0.021455682814121246, 0.012442992068827152, -0.011953880079090595, -0.005826945882290602, 0.04523301497101784, -0.013721202500164509, 0.025851164013147354, -0.002337952144443989, -0.003837893484160304, -0.0058693359605968, -0.008406192995607853, -0.012169089168310165, -0.006609524134546518, 0.010499589145183563, 0.017125416547060013, -0.02428600750863552, 0.009553974494338036, -0.023594729602336884, -0.006156281102448702, 0.004284615162760019, -0.0031123782973736525, -0.0026656566187739372, -0.01779060810804367, 0